  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sanjay Chaudhary vs Bharat Bhushan Patel on 28 March, 2025 1 Digitally signed by Avinash Avinash Sharma",
    "facts": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that complaint filed by the respondent is barred by limitation under Section 77 of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (henceforth \"the Act, 2006\"). He further submits that perusal of order sheets dated from 06.04.2018 to 09.11.2023 of the trial Court would show that complainant was not aware as to the name of the accused. On perusal of record, this Court finds that complainant has filed a complaint case against the petitioners under Section 26(1), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(v), 27(3)(c), 27(2)(c) and Section 31 of the Act, 2006. It is also found that complaint case has been filed on 06.04.2018. However, name of the owner/proprietor of Seeta Enterprises has not been mentioned and complainant sought time to file correct name of owner/proprietor of Seeta Enterprises. Order sheets annexed with the petition go to show that the trial Court has given several dates to the complainant for the purpose of providing name of the owner/proprietor of Seeta Enterprises, for taking cognizance on 26.04.2018, 31.05.2018, 27.06.2018, 28.08.2018, 12.10.2018, 27.12.2018, 23.01.2019, 18.02.2019, 20.3.2019, 29.04.2019, 29.05.2019, 25.07.2019, 11.09.2019, 17.10.2019, 26.11.2019, 24.01.2020, 14.02.2020, 20.05.2020, 18.11.2020, 22.01.2021, 23.03.2021, 09.07.2021, 04.10.2021, 14.12.2021, 26.02.2022, 12.05.2022, 10.08.2022, 21.10.2022, 29.12.2022, 16.03.2023, 14.06.2023, 07.09.2023 and 10.10.2023. On these dates which amount to nearly 5 years, complainant has not provided the name of owner/proprietor of Seeta Enterprises, therefore, learned trial Court has not taken cognizance within a period of 5 years. Under Section 77 of the Act, 2006, wherein, one year is prescribed for taking cognizance--against the petitioners after name of concerned owner/proprietor was provided by the complainant.",
